---
import { skillsExplorer as app } from '../data/skillsExplorer';
const screenshots = [
  ['workbench', 'Read skills and follow references', 'The skill tree and colored reader keep files, links and related skills together.'],
  ['metadata', 'Inspect metadata and file size', 'Frontmatter, dates, file counts, context estimates and available telemetry, with their sources.'],
  ['commands', 'Find a command without memorizing it', 'Search the same command catalog used by the menus, including Deep Eval Optimizer routes.'],
  ['hotkeys', 'Keep every shortcut within reach', 'The scrollable help reference covers application commands and native widget navigation.'],
];
const options = [
  ['--help', 'Show all command-line options.'],
  ['--version', 'Print the installed version.'],
  ['--root HARNESS=PATH', 'Use only the specified roots. Repeat for multiple roots; labels identify them in the tree.'],
  ['--home PATH', 'Choose the configuration, cache, backups and results directory.'],
  ['--list', 'Print a fresh skill inventory as JSON without opening the TUI.'],
  ['--eval SKILL_PATH', 'Run a saved evaluation suite for a skill file or directory in the configured roots.'],
];
const shortcuts = [
  ['Arrows · Tab / Shift+Tab', 'Navigate skills, files, menus and controls. Down opens a collapsed dropdown or tree node; otherwise it moves down.'],
  ['? · F1', 'Show all hotkeys. Use F1 from a text input; ? remains ordinary punctuation there.'],
  ['Ctrl+P', 'Focus command search. Type a command, press Enter or Down, then select a result.'],
  ['Alt+E / Alt+O / Alt+G / Alt+H', 'Open Edit, Optimize, GitHub or Help. Escape goes back or closes a menu.'],
  ['/', 'Focus skill search; in a dropdown, focus its command filter.'],
  ['r · e · Ctrl+D', 'Refresh all skills, edit SKILL.md, or enable/disable the selected installation.'],
  ['o · v · a · Delete', 'Clean up formatting, run evaluations, add a skill, or move a skill to recoverable trash.'],
  ['Ctrl+Q', 'Quit the workbench.'],
];
---
<section id="skills-explorer" class="skills-explorer-download" aria-labelledby="skills-explorer-heading">
  <p class="eyebrow">Local terminal application · v{app.version} · MIT license</p>
  <h2 id="skills-explorer-heading">Skills Explorer</h2>
  <p class="lead">Browse, edit, optimize and evaluate your installed agent skills from one terminal workbench.</p>
  <p>Skills Explorer reads your local <code>SKILL.md</code> libraries across Claude, Codex,
    shared agents and other harnesses. Explore a skill's supporting files and references,
    inspect its metadata, and manage its installation without switching between directories.
    It is a companion to the <code>llmsx</code> concept-tree explorer: use Skills Explorer
    for your installed skills, and <code>llmsx explorer</code> for the research concept tree.</p>
  <p class="hero-actions">
    <a class="btn" href="#skills-explorer-install">Install &amp; launch</a>
    <a class="btn secondary" href={app.release}>GitHub release</a>
    <a class="btn secondary" href={app.source}>Download source</a>
  </p>
  <nav class="section-nav" aria-label="Skills Explorer guide">
    <a href="#skills-explorer-screenshots">Screenshots</a>
    <a href="#skills-explorer-features">Features</a>
    <a href="#skills-explorer-install">Installation</a>
    <a href="#skills-explorer-setup">Setup</a>
    <a href="#skills-explorer-usage">Usage &amp; hotkeys</a>
    <a href="#skills-explorer-options">CLI options</a>
  </nav>

  <h3 id="skills-explorer-screenshots">A look inside</h3>
  <div class="screenshots">
    {screenshots.map(([file, title, caption]) => (
      <figure>
        <a href={`/images/skills-explorer/${file}.svg`} aria-label={`Open full-size screenshot: ${title}`}>
          <img src={`/images/skills-explorer/${file}.svg`} alt={`${title}. ${caption}`}
            width="1482" height="1026" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
        </a>
        <figcaption><strong>{title}</strong><br />{caption}</figcaption>
      </figure>
    ))}
  </div>
  <p class="note">Captured from the application with a small example library. Select an image to view it at full size.</p>

  <h3 id="skills-explorer-features">What you can do</h3>
  <dl class="features">
    <div><dt>Explore and search</dt><dd>Browse multiple harnesses and roots, search by name, description or path,
      and follow local references. Files and referenced children load as you expand them. Sort by name,
      modification, local creation date, size, observed invocation count or last observed access.</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Edit and organize</dt><dd>Create or edit skills with backups, enable or disable an installation,
      restore recoverable trash, add roots, and rehome a skill into an existing parent router. The rehome
      workflow prepares the parent routing changes and peer seeding through your installed tree architect.</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Optimize from a menu</dt><dd>Use the SkillOpt submenu to optimize, dry-run, harvest, review status, adopt a proposal, schedule or unschedule. Or launch custom
      skills including Deep Skill Optimizer (<code>/sko</code>), Deep Prompt Optimizer (<code>/pdo</code>),
      skill-tree-architect and skill-refresher. Formatting cleanup is built in; native workflows use
      your installed skills and configured runners.</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Evaluate and improve</dt><dd>Create, edit and run evaluation suites. The Evaluations submenu includes
      Deep Eval Optimizer routes and an eval-agent launcher. Choose the <code>/deo</code> wrapper or direct skill route; configure <code>--audit</code>, <code>--create</code>, <code>--run</code>, <code>--dry-run</code>, <code>--eval-type</code> and <code>--max-iter</code>. Review the target, options and runner
      before starting a workflow; these integrations require the corresponding installed skill or agent.</dd></div>
    <div><dt>See the evidence</dt><dd>Read frontmatter and metadata sidecars, filesystem dates, per-file lines,
      characters and bytes, total footprint, and available usage and optimizer history. Context tokens
      are character-based estimates. Runtime tokens require telemetry; missing observations display
      “Unavailable.” Local file creation is separate from original authorship.</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Stay oriented</dt><dd>Edit, Optimize, GitHub and Help menus share a searchable command catalog.
      Links and paths are blue, timestamps yellow, headings green and skill slugs purple. Cached skill
      rows appear on repeat launches, a background refresh runs on load, and file changes trigger
      another refresh. The first launch creates the cache.</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Work with GitHub</dt><dd>Open the bundled GitHub control panel to browse commands from your installed
      <code>gh</code> CLI, or connect and sync a skill library. GitHub actions run only when you explicitly
      execute a command.</dd></div>
  </dl>

  <h3 id="skills-explorer-install">Install and launch</h3>
  <p>Choose one installation method. Both <code>skillsx</code> and <code>skills-explorer</code> launch the same
    application. A terminal at least 120 columns by 35 rows is recommended.</p>
  <h4>Homebrew</h4>
  <p>On macOS or Linux with <a href="https://brew.sh/">Homebrew</a>, install from the project's public tap.
    Homebrew installs the Python runtime and dependencies.</p>
  <pre><code>{`brew install mithudso/tap/skills-explorer
skillsx`}</code></pre>
  <h4>npm package</h4>
  <p>Requires Node.js 18+ and <a href="https://docs.astral.sh/uv/getting-started/installation/">uv on your PATH</a>.
    Install the published <a href="https://www.npmjs.com/package/skills-explorer">npm package</a>:</p>
  <pre><code>{`npm install -g skills-explorer
skillsx`}</code></pre>
  <p>Or run it without a global npm installation:</p>
  <pre><code>{`npx skills-explorer`}</code></pre>
  <p>The npm package includes the application wheels. At first launch, uv prepares a cached, isolated
    Python 3.11+ environment and fetches its pinned dependencies; internet access is required for
    that setup. The package has no install hook.</p>
  <h4>Python source</h4>
  <p>Download and extract the <a href={app.source}>source archive</a>, then enter its directory.
    Install with uv and Python 3.11+:</p>
  <pre><code>{`cd skills-explorer-${app.version}
uv tool install --with ./modules/github-control-panel .
skillsx`}</code></pre>
  <p>The source archive includes the GitHub control panel. The <a href={app.release}>release page</a>
    also provides wheels and SHA-256 checksums. The <a href={app.github}>public GitHub repository</a>
    hosts the Homebrew formula, releases and issue tracker.</p>

  <h3 id="skills-explorer-setup">Set up your library</h3>
  <p>Run <code>skillsx</code> from your project directory to discover supported user and project roots.
    Discovery includes Claude, Codex, shared <code>.agents</code>, Gemini, Cursor, OpenCode,
    OpenClaw, Windsurf, Copilot and Amp locations, plus Claude/Codex plugin caches. Missing directories
    are skipped. Plugin roots are read-only. To choose your own scope:</p>
  <pre><code>{`skillsx --root "Claude=$HOME/.claude/skills" --root "Codex=$HOME/.codex/skills"
skillsx --root "Project=$PWD/.agents/skills"`}</code></pre>
  <p>Use <strong>Edit → Add root</strong> for another local or mounted library, and <strong>Edit → Settings</strong>
    to configure optional integrations. State, inventory cache, backups, trash and results live in
    <code>~/.local/share/skills-explorer</code> by default. Set <code>SKILLSX_HOME</code> or pass
    <code>--home</code> to choose another directory.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Browsing and editing:</strong> work locally without an API key.</li>
    <li><strong>GitHub:</strong> install <a href="https://cli.github.com/">GitHub CLI</a> and authenticate
      with <code>gh auth login</code> before using authenticated commands. Set your own library remote in Settings.</li>
    <li><strong>Native optimizer skills:</strong> install and authenticate Claude Code, and install the
      matching commands or skills. SkillOpt uses a separately installed SkillOpt backend.</li>
    <li><strong>Eval agent:</strong> supply the exact name of an installed Claude agent in its launch form.
      An agent definition is not bundled.</li>
    <li><strong>External runners and usage:</strong> configure runner argument arrays and an optional usage
      JSONL path in Settings. Invocations, reference reads and token measurements remain attributed to their sources.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3 id="skills-explorer-usage">Use the workbench</h3>
  <ol>
    <li>Launch <code>skillsx</code>. The first skill is selected and previewed.</li>
    <li>Search or sort the list, then use arrows to expand a skill, supporting files or references.</li>
    <li>Switch between Read, Source, Metadata and Results. Use the menus or command search to choose an action.</li>
    <li>Press <kbd>?</kbd> for the complete shortcut reference. Refresh with <kbd>r</kbd> at any time.</li>
  </ol>
  <div class="table-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Skills Explorer keyboard shortcuts">
    <table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Key</th><th scope="col">Action</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>{shortcuts.map(([key, action]) => <tr><td><kbd>{key}</kbd></td><td>{action}</td></tr>)}</tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p class="note">Text inputs retain their typing keys and editors retain native cursor navigation. Arrows navigate menus;
    Enter selects an action. The in-app Help menu lists every context-specific shortcut.</p>

  <h3 id="skills-explorer-options">Command-line options</h3>
  <div class="table-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Skills Explorer command-line options">
    <table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Option</th><th scope="col">Behavior</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>{options.map(([option, behavior]) => <tr><td><code>{option}</code></td><td>{behavior}</td></tr>)}</tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <pre><code>{`# Fresh JSON inventory
skillsx --root "Project=$PWD/.agents/skills" --list

# Separate state and saved evaluation suite
skillsx --home "$HOME/.skillsx-demo" --root "Project=$PWD/.agents/skills"
skillsx --root "Project=$PWD/.agents/skills" --eval "$PWD/.agents/skills/example/SKILL.md"

# Check your installation
skillsx --version
skillsx --help`}</code></pre>
</section>
<style>
  .skills-explorer-download { scroll-margin-top: 7rem; margin: var(--sp-7) 0; padding-top: var(--sp-5); border-top: 2px solid var(--accent); }
  .eyebrow { font-size: .8rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .07em; color: var(--accent); }
  .lead { font-size: 1.25rem; }
  h2 { margin-top: var(--sp-2); }
  h3 { margin-top: var(--sp-7); scroll-margin-top: 7rem; }
  h4 { margin-top: var(--sp-5); }
  .section-nav { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: var(--sp-3) var(--sp-5); padding: var(--sp-4) 0; border-block: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .screenshots { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: var(--sp-5); }
  figure { margin: 0; min-width: 0; }
  img { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; background: #0c1021; border-radius: var(--radius); }
  figcaption { margin-top: var(--sp-2); font-size: .9rem; color: var(--ink-muted); }
  figcaption strong { color: var(--ink); }
  .note { color: var(--ink-muted); font-size: .85rem; }
  .features { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: var(--sp-5); }
  .features > div { padding: var(--sp-4); background: var(--paper-raised); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: var(--radius); }
  dt { font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: var(--sp-2); }
  dd { margin: 0; }
  li { margin-bottom: var(--sp-2); }
  pre { max-width: 100%; overflow-x: auto; }
  p, dd, li { overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
  .table-scroll { max-width: 100%; overflow-x: auto; }
  table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; }
  th, td { padding: var(--sp-3); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); text-align: left; vertical-align: top; }
  th { background: var(--accent-soft); }
  td:first-child { width: 31%; }
  td code, td kbd { overflow-wrap: anywhere; white-space: normal; }
  @media (max-width: 680px) { .screenshots, .features { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
</style>
